1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,310
Your cat meows at you, but almost never at other cats.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,080
Kittens meow when they're cold or hungry,

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,650
so their mother comes running.

4
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:12,090
Adult cats grow out of it and talk with scent and body language instead.

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,410
Except with us.

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,590
Humans kept answering, so cats kept the kitten voice.

7
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:17,890
And they tuned it.

8
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:22,300
In one study, cats begging for food hid a cry inside their purr,

9
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,800
near the pitch of a crying baby,

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,010
and people found it hard to ignore.

11
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:29,230
Every cat learns which meows work on its human.

12
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:30,660
So at five in the morning,

13
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:31,800
when the bowl is empty,
